ed blobs","url":"https://github.com/serde-rs/serde/pull/2590","score":64,"flags":4,"comment_count":100,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"alanz","user_is_author":false,"tags":["rust"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/sgoshm","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/sgoshm/serde_is_no_longer_shipping_precompiled"},{"short_id":"vlmsti","created_at":"2023-08-28T07:03:52.000-05:00","title":"From tui-rs to Ratatui: 6 Months of Cooking Up Rust TUIs","url":"https://blog.orhun.dev/ratatui-0-23-0/","score":26,"flags":1,"comment_count":0,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"orhun","user_is_author":true,"tags":["programming","rust"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/vlmsti","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/vlmsti/from_tui_rs_ratatui_6_months_cooking_up"},{"short_id":"j8unbh","created_at":"2023-08-28T06:17:40.000-05:00","title":"What are some cool side projects you have planned but haven't gotten around to doing?","url":"","score":8,"flags":0,"comment_count":22,"description":"\u003cp\u003eLike \u003ca href=\"https://lobste.rs/s/c5comj/what_are_some_cool_side_projects_you_have\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003ethis thread\u003c/a\u003e, but for the stuff you'll \"get around to any day now\".\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"Like [this thread](https://lobste.rs/s/c5comj/what_are_some_cool_side_projects_you_have), but for the stuff you'll \"get around to any day now\".","submitter_user":"teh_codez","user_is_author":true,"tags":["ask","programming"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/j8unbh","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/j8unbh/what_are_some_cool_side_projects_you_have"},{"short_id":"xyaxjo","created_at":"2023-08-28T06:14:24.000-05:00","title":"A Taxonomy of Bugs","url":"https://ruby0x1.github.io/machinery_blog_archive/post/a-taxonomy-of-bugs/index.html","score":3,"flags":0,"comment_count":1,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"signal-11","user_is_author":false,"tags":["api","debugging","programming"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/xyaxjo","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/xyaxjo/taxonomy_bugs"},{"short_id":"fyvcsx","created_at":"2023-08-28T06:11:19.000-05:00","title":"First Postgres Vector Extension with Filtering Support","url":"https://modelz.ai/blog/pgvecto-rs-condition-filtering","score":1,"flags":0,"comment_count":0,"description":"\u003cp\u003eHi,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn our previous post titled \"Do we really need a specialized vector database?\" on HN (\u003ca href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=37097004\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003ehttps://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=37097004\u003c/a\u003e) we discussed the importance of using a Postgres-based solution for vector search. However, we acknowledged that existing Postgres vector extensions lack support for metadata filtering.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe are excited to announce that we have now addressed this limitation. We are proud to be the first (\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/tensorchord/pgvecto.rs\" rel=\"ugc\"\u003ehttps://github.com/tensorchord/pgvecto.rs\u003c/a\u003e) to enable conditional filtering directly on HNSW indexes within Postgres. This breakthrough allows for efficient and effective metadata filtering in combination with vector search, eliminating the tradeoff previously associated with using Postgres for this purpose.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe invite you to explore our updated offering and experience the benefits of seamless metadata filtering within a Postgres-based vector search system.\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"Hi,\r\n\r\nIn our previous post titled \"Do we really need a specialized vector database?\" on HN (https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=37097004) we discussed the importance of using a Postgres-based solution for vector search. However, we acknowledged that existing Postgres vector extensions lack support for metadata filtering.\r\n\r\nWe are excited to announce that we have now addressed this limitation. We are proud to be the first (https://github.com/tensorchord/pgvecto.rs) to enable conditional filtering directly on HNSW indexes within Postgres. This breakthrough allows for efficient and effective metadata filtering in combination with vector search, eliminating the tradeoff previously associated with using Postgres for this purpose.\r\n\r\nWe invite you to explore our updated offering and experience the benefits of seamless metadata filtering within a Postgres-based vector search system.","submitter_user":"gaocegege","user_is_author":true,"tags":["ai","databases","rust"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/fyvcsx","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/fyvcsx/first_postgres_vector_extension_with"},{"short_id":"xir7l8","created_at":"2023-08-28T05:53:21.000-05:00","title":"What are you doing this week?","url":"","score":7,"flags":0,"comment_count":8,"description":"\u003cp\u003eWhat are you doing this week? Feel free to share!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKeep in mind it’s OK to do nothing at all, too.\u003c/p\u003e\n","description_plain":"What are you doing this week? Feel free to share!\r\n\r\nKeep in mind it’s OK to do nothing at all, too.","submitter_user":"caius","user_is_author":true,"tags":["ask","programming"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/xir7l8","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/xir7l8/what_are_you_doing_this_week"},{"short_id":"uumm5j","created_at":"2023-08-28T02:30:43.000-05:00","title":"Nix revisited","url":"https://lottia.net/notes/0003-nix-revisited.html","score":38,"flags":0,"comment_count":51,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"kivikakk","user_is_author":true,"tags":["nix"],"short_id_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/uumm5j","comments_url":"https://lobste.rs/s/uumm5j/nix_revisited"},{"short_id":"17beun","created_at":"2023-08-28T02:06:02.000-05:00","title":"Learning programming with a turtle","url":"https://anto.pt/articles/learning-programming-with-a-turtle","score":14,"flags":0,"comment_count":7,"description":"","description_plain":"","submitter_user":"zaphodias","user_is_author":tr